  "rationale": "No supported optimization applies without contraindication. Go module dependency caching is already provided by actions/setup-go@v6 with cache-dependency-path: src/go.sum in both jobs, so adding actions/cache@v4 for ~/go/pkg/mod would be redundant (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE contraindication: an equivalent cache already exists). The postgres-regressions job already defines timeout-minutes: 30. Adding a custom timeout to the compile job is not supported by evidence of an appropriate duration; the job performs sudo apt install plus make release, and valid slow runs could exceed an arbitrary limit (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT contraindication: valid slow runs exceed the proposed limit). No other pattern fits without weakening coverage or adding unrelated changes.",
  "evidence_ids": ["pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "pattern:P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "experiment:batch-interactive-three--f6d2974a5cef7cc9", "experiment:batch-interactive-three--112e2b2e7fbe04b8"]
